1 NOTE {geni:about_me} José Téllez Girón, I, and Catalina Romero had three sons who were adults in 1681: '''José, II''', Juan and Rafael. Two of his known daughters were María, who married Diego de Medina, and Isabel, who became the wife
2 CONC  of Jacinto Sánches.
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of New Mexico families, pg. 106
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Chávez, Fray Angélico, Origins of New Mexico Families: A Genealogy of the Spanish Colonial Period, Rev. Ed. ISBN 978-0-89013-239-5 (Santa Fe: Museum of New Mexico Press, 1992.)
