1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Raul Longoria's Genealogy Database:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.raullongoria.net/Genealogy/FamilyTree/b105.html#P1914
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Margarita GONZALES [119],[513],[2072] 
2 CONT *was born (date unknown). 
2 CONT *Margarita Gonzales, widow of an original settler of Camargo, was the Original Grantee of Porcion 103. This was one of only nine Porciones in Camargo that had no access to the Rio Grande River. [The surveyors who laid out the porc
2 CONC iones had started at the boundary with Mier and worked downriver to the boundary with Reynosa but still needed to site nine more porciones; hence their location away from the river.] Porcion 103 contained 6,218.26 acres and is sit
2 CONC uated in present-day Starr County, Texas.
2 CONT *Spouse: Juan Crisostomo HINOJOSA. Maria Margarita GONZALES and Juan Crisostomo HINOJOSA were married. Children were: 
2 CONT **1. Maria Rita HINOJOSA Gonzales, 
2 CONT **2. Maria Gertrudis HINOJOSA Gonzales, 
2 CONT **3. Candida HINOJOSA Gonzales, 
2 CONT **4. Jose de HINOJOSA Gonzales, 
2 CONT **5. Bernarda HINOJOSA Gonzales, 
2 CONT **6. Diego HINOJOSA Gonzales, 
2 CONT **7. Maria Ygnacia HINOJOSA Gonzales.
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes:
2 CONT *119. Family Tree Book (The F. W. Seabury Papers), a transcription of the original papers in The Center for American History at The University of Texas at Austin, transcribed and edited by Joel Rene Escobar, New Santander Press, E
2 CONC dinburg, TX, 1995, page 367.
2 CONT *513. Family Tree Book (The F. W. Seabury Papers), a transcription of the original papers in The Center for American History at The University of Texas at Austin, transcribed and edited by Joel Rene Escobar, New Santander Press, E
2 CONC dinburg, TX, 1995, page 460.
2 CONT *2072. Greaser, New Guide to Spanish and Mexican Land Grants in South Texas, page 250.
