1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Los Origens De La Familia Olivares by Zacarias Joel Olivarez (webcached 2/2/2013):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/o/l/i/Zacarias--J-Olivarez/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0400.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonio De Olivares 
2 CONT *(son of Blas De Olivares and Maria Ramona Escandon) was born 1716 in Cerralvo Mexico, and 
2 CONT *died date unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Antonio De Olivares was the brother of Don Tomas De Olivares. Antonio was the grantee of Land Grant # 36. (Porcion 36) which is located one land grant away from Tomas' grant. Don Bernardo Ynojosa (Hinojosa) also later took pos
2 CONC session of Joseph Antonio Gonzalez's and then sold it to Don Tomas De Olivares. Therefore,Tomas had two Land Grants, Porcion 34 which was given to him by the King of Spain, and Porcion 8 which he later bought. Both of them ran Eas
2 CONC t to West on the South side of the Rio Grande River. (In Mexico this river is called El Rio Bravo del Norte).
