1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Los Origens De La Familia Olivares by Zacarias Joel Olivarez (webcached 2/2/2013):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/o/l/i/Zacarias--J-Olivarez/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0034.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Tomas De Olivares 
2 CONT *(son of Blas De Olivares and Maria Ramona Escandon) was born Abt. 1725 in Saltillo Mexico, and 
2 CONT *died 04 May 1814 in Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mexico. 
2 CONT *He married Gertrudis Estefana Longoria on Abt. 1758 in Camargo Mexico, 
2 CONT **daughter of Cpt. Juan Diego Longoria Garcia and Maria Chapa Baez Benavidez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Tomas De Olivares was born in Saltillo Mexico. He was the son of Blas De Olivares and Maria Ramona Escandon. She was related to Jose De Escandon, the General given the credit for the largest migratory expedition to settle the 
2 CONC northern borders of Mexico, which included Texas (Tejas). His expedition was larger then the expedition of the Mormans who settled in the Utah area hundred or more years later. You can find out more about Jose De Escandon's amazin
2 CONC g story in the internet by typing his name or by going to http://www.rootweb.com/~mextam/escand01.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Tomas De Olivarez was granted Porcion 34 (Land Grant #34) which he named RANCHO LA BONITA. It is located near Camargo Mexico, closer to a small village called Comales Mexico. Comales is about 17 miles south southwest of Camargo Me
2 CONC xico. Camargo is across the Border from Rio Grande City Texas. Part of Tomas' land grant is now under water due to the building of a Dam named after General Trevino. His brother Antonio De Olivares was awarded Porcion 36, just a f
2 CONC ew miles from Tomas' land. Don Bernardo Ynojosa took possession of Porcion 8 that first belonged to Joseph Antonio Gonzalez. He then sold it to Don Tomas De Olivares. Therefore, Tomas had two Land Grants, Porcion 34 which was give
2 CONC n to him by the King of Spain, and Porcion 8 which he later bought. Both of them ran East to West on the South side of the Rio Grande River. (In Mexico this river is called El Rio Bravo del Norte)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a Museum dedicated to Tomas in the small town of Comales Mexico. It is run by the Garcia Family. They are related to the brother and sister team of Garcias that married the son and daughter of Tomas, Francisco and Gertrud
2 CONC is Olivares. Francisco marred Josefa Garcia and Gertrudis married Pedro Ygnacio Garcia. They descend from Pedro and Gertrudis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Tomas De Olivares and Gertrudis Estefana Longoria:
2 CONT *Marriage: Abt. 1758, Camargo Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Tomas De Olivares and Gertrudis Estefana Longoria are:
2 CONT *1. +Francisco Jose De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1765, Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mx., 
2 CONT **d. date unknown.
2 CONT *2. +Maria Gertrudis De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. 13 Jul 1767, Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1795, Camargo Mexico.
2 CONT *3. +Alejandro De Olivares, 
2 CONT **b. Abt. 1772, Rancho La Bonita near Camargo Mexico, 
2 CONT **d. Abt. 1840, Rancho La Bonita Mexico.
